-- title:
--   H BConsistency Fixed U Defect Le Avg Over Distinct
-- statement:
--   **The fixed-base-point pasted defect is bounded by the distinct-tuple average.**
--
--   Let `params`, `strategy`, and `family` satisfy the field and strategy hypotheses, let $k\in\mathbb{N}$, and fix a base point $u$. The vertical restriction defect of the constructed pasted submeasurement is at most the average over pairwise distinct height tuples:
--
--   $$
--   \operatorname{qBipartiteConsDefect}\left(\operatorname{hRestrictionToVerticalLine}(\operatorname{constructedPastedSubMeas},u),\operatorname{verticalLineMeasurementFamily}(u)\right)\le\operatorname{avgOver}_{xs\sim\operatorname{distinctTupleDistribution}(\mathrm{params},k)}\operatorname{qBipartiteConsDefect}\left(\operatorname{hRestrictionToVerticalLine}(\operatorname{pastedInterpolationFamily}(xs),u),\operatorname{verticalLineMeasurementFamily}(u)\right).
--   $$
--
--   This follows from the average representation of the pasted submeasurement and convexity of the consistency defect.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.hBConsistency_fixed_u_defect_le_avgOver_distinct`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
